RETURN v from a handler responds 200 with v as JSON, and maps keep insertion
order (Requirement 7.5, 3.5).

### a map, keys in the order they were set
GET /map
=> 200

{"b": 2, "a": 1, "z": "last"}

### an array
POST /array
=> 200

[1, 2.5, "three", true, null]

### a value built by another function
DELETE /nested
=> 200

{"method": "DELETE", "list": [{"x": 1}, []]}
